{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: permanently-rejected zombies retry (and warn) every tick forever — no E2 escalation path**

A rejection that can never succeed — most notably a terminal-owner check-run created by a *different* GitHub App (the gh-865 detector is not filtered to this app's own check-runs, so a third-party integration's orphaned check-run lands in `vOrphans` too) — makes GitHub 403/404 the PATCH on every tick, producing a `⚠️ zombie sweep rejected` warn per PR per tick with no progress and no alarm. Transient failures benefit from the retry, but permanent ones become log noise that masks real signal.

The ticket's E2 also asks for "a persistent failure escalates to an issue (existing alarm path) rather than silently leaking." Suggest a follow-up: bound the retries per check-run id (e.g. reject the same id N ticks in a row → post one tracker comment via the existing alarm path, then mark-and-skip it), so the sweep stays actionable instead of chatty. Fine as a separate card — does not block this PR.","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: GH_TOKEN restore depends on `sourceToken` being present — otherwise the app token leaks into the rest of the tick**

The `finally` restores `GH_TOKEN` only when `swapped && sourceTok`. If `jobParams.silentToken` is set but `sourceToken` is absent (optional param), the sweep leaves `GH_TOKEN` swapped to the workflow app token after returning, and every subsequent `gh`/CLI call in the tick runs under the app identity instead of the source identity — a subtle privilege/identity drift that is hard to diagnose from logs.

This mirrors the pre-existing gh-857 `concludePlaceholderCheckRuns` pattern, so it's not a regression, but a new transport is the cheap place to harden: snapshot the pre-swap `GH_TOKEN` value (e.g. `env GH_TOKEN` before swapping) and restore that snapshot in the `finally` instead of relying on `sourceToken`, e.g.:

```javascript
var prevTok = null;
try { prevTok = /* read GH_TOKEN */; } catch (e0) {}
...
} finally {
    if (swapped) {
        try {
            if (prevTok) set_env_variable('GH_TOKEN', prevTok);
            else set_env_variable_unset('GH_TOKEN'); // or platform equivalent
        } catch (e3) {}
    }
}
```","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment3.md"}

